  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "In Europe, the brands most often considered for **upper-upscale hotel conversions** fall into two groups: flexible collection/soft brands and conventional full-service brands that accept conversions.\n\n| Hotel group | Common conversion candidates | Typical fit |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Marriott International** | **Autograph Collection**, **Tribute Portfolio** | Leading soft-brand options for distinctive independent hotels |\n|  | Renaissance, Sheraton, Le Méridien, Westin, Delta Hotels | More standardized conversions where the physical product can meet brand requirements |\n| **Hilton** | **Curio Collection by Hilton**, **DoubleTree by Hilton** | Curio preserves individuality; DoubleTree is a widely used conventional conversion flag |\n|  | Hilton Hotels & Resorts | Larger full-service assets, subject to stronger brand compliance |\n| **IHG** | **voco**, **Noted Collection** | Both specifically oriented toward conversion; Noted targets upscale-to-upper-upscale independents |\n|  | Crowne Plaza, Hotel Indigo | Business/conference hotels and design-led urban properties, respectively |\n|  | Vignette Collection | Generally for higher-end upper-upscale or luxury independent hotels |\n| **Accor** | **MGallery Collection**, Pullman | Frequently considered for boutique/lifestyle and large full-service assets |\n|  | Swissôtel, Mövenpick, Grand Mercure | Market-dependent premium/upper-upscale alternatives |\n| **Radisson Hotel Group** | **Radisson Blu** | One of Europe’s most established upper-upscale conversion flags |\n|  | Radisson Collection, Park Plaza, art’otel | Higher-end, major-city or lifestyle properties |\n|  | Radisson Individuals | Flexible soft-brand solution, although some hotels trade closer to upscale |\n| **Hyatt** | **The Unbound Collection by Hyatt** | Principal flexible option for distinctive upper-upscale and luxury conversions |\n|  | Hyatt Regency, Hyatt Centric | Conventional full-service or lifestyle conversions where market coverage supports them |\n| **Minor Hotels** | **NH Collection**, nhow | Strong European recognition, especially in Southern and Continental Europe |\n|  | Tivoli Hotels & Resorts | Higher-end urban and resort conversions |\n| **Wyndham** | Dolce Hotels & Resorts by Wyndham, Wyndham Grand | Particularly relevant for conference, resort and large full-service properties |\n|  | Trademark Collection | Flexible collection brand, though positioning ranges from upscale to upper-upscale |\n| **H World/Deutsche Hospitality** | MAXX by Steigenberger, Steigenberger Hotels & Resorts | Particularly relevant in Germany, Austria, Switzerland and parts of Central Europe |\n\n### Most common initial shortlist\n\nFor a typical European independent four-star-superior or five-star conversion, the brands most likely to make an initial screening are:\n\n1. **Autograph Collection**\n2. **Tribute Portfolio**\n3. **Curio Collection**\n4. **DoubleTree by Hilton**\n5. **voco**\n6. **Noted Collection**\n7. **MGallery**\n8. **Pullman**\n9. **Radisson Blu**\n10. **NH Collection**\n11. **The Unbound Collection by Hyatt**\n12. **Crowne Plaza**\n\nMarriott identifies Autograph Collection and Tribute Portfolio as important drivers of its European premium conversion pipeline. IHG positions voco as a premium conversion brand and launched Noted Collection in February 2026 specifically for upscale-to-upper-upscale conversions. Radisson describes Radisson Blu as Europe’s largest upper-upscale brand, while Hilton explicitly promotes DoubleTree as suited to European conversion properties. ([marriott-international.pressarea.com](https://marriott-international.pressarea.com/en/pressrelease/details/19580?utm_source=openai))\n\nThe right shortlist ultimately depends on **location, room count and size, meeting space, F&B configuration, renovation capex, existing identity, franchise versus management preference, and territorial availability**. Also, chain-scale classifications are not completely uniform: a brand may be described as “premium,” “upscale,” or “upper-upscale” depending on the operator, market and benchmarking provider.",
